Description: Analysis and reporting pipeline for cell culture assays read
    out by microscopy, starting from segmented single-cell exports such as
    those written by 'segmantR', 'CellProfiler' or 'QuPath'. Recovers the
    experimental design from the directory tree and the file naming
    convention, resolves acquisitions into the analysis unit of
    replication, and standardizes every cell against the control
    condition of its own batch. Applies threshold and biological quality
    control gates, then estimates effect sizes with confidence intervals
    at both unit and cell level so that the cost of treating cells as
    replicates is visible rather than assumed. Sample sizes for a
    follow-up study are solved from the confidence bound nearer the null
    instead of the observed point estimate, after Cohen (1988,
    ISBN:9780805802832). Figures, machine-readable tables and a generated
    file of every quoted number are emitted from the same objects, and an
    interactive 'shiny' application provides guided analysis and report
    export.
